    "article_title_3": "Batteries and charging",
    "article_3_intro": "The number of batteries, the charging setup and their care decide how much the drone can work in a day.",
    "article_3_h1": "How many batteries you need",
    "article_3_p1": "The drone flies while the next battery charges. Flight time and charging time have to match, so larger areas need more batteries and chargers. We will choose the right number for your area and working day together.",
    "article_3_h2": "Power in the field",
    "article_3_p2": "There is not always mains power in the field. A generator and a parallel charging kit let you charge where you work. Use the equipment the manufacturer recommends.",
    "article_3_h3": "Cooling and temperature",
    "article_3_p3": "On a hot day a battery warms up in flight. Cool it before charging, for example with a cooling tank. Charging a hot battery shortens its life.",
    "article_3_h4": "Storage between seasons",
    "article_3_p4": "After the season, store batteries in a dry, cool place at the charge level the manufacturer specifies. Do not use a damaged or swollen battery.",
    "article_title_4": "Service and parts",
    "article_4_intro": "In season, even one day of downtime is expensive. Service and parts close by keep that time short.",
    "article_4_h1": "Pre-season check",
    "article_4_p1": "Before the season, check the motors, propellers, pumps, nozzles and cables. A small fault found early saves a long stop in the field.",
    "article_4_h2": "Original parts",
    "article_4_p2": "A non-original part can change how the drone works and how safe it is. Original XAG parts for the P150 MAX are in stock in our warehouse in Georgia.",
    "article_4_h3": "Regular care",
    "article_4_p3": "After every working day, rinse the spraying system and inspect the drone. Follow the manufacturer’s manual or ask our team about care routines.",
    "article_4_h4": "When something is not right",
    "article_4_p4": "If the drone shows a warning or behaves strangely, stop flying and contact us. We do the diagnostics and repairs ourselves.",
    "about_story_3": "Our current focus is the XAG P150 MAX. We provide the full XAG ecosystem: drones, batteries, chargers, generators, parts, service and training — for farmers, service companies and government and municipal buyers.",
